{
  "//": "Where each test file of verify-container.sh --tests runs (CT-06zzzzz, D10-1319 / D10-1334; the same format as red-projects.json, read by tools/ops/red-plan.ts --projects). First every project of red-projects.json, unchanged and in its order (--red keeps using red-projects.json alone); then one project per Vitest config of the packages: apps/api and packages/db unit (vitest.config.ts) and integration (vitest.integration.config.ts, database: true), apps/admin, apps/h5, packages/bridge-sdk, contracts-ts, domain, money, ui-tokens and tools unit. include / exclude mirror each config with the defaults of unitConfig / integrationConfig in vitest.shared.ts, relative to `dir` (BASE_EXCLUDE left out, as in red-projects.json); unit projects leave *.int.test.ts out, so every file has one project. test/vitest.longrun.config.ts is not here. tools/ops/red-plan.test.ts fails when a config and this table disagree. A browser project stops --tests (browser tests run with --browser). `name` names the out/<name>.* files. Trusted file (protected path, class 3).",
  "projects": [
    {
      "name": "spec-unit",
      "dir": "test",
      "config": "vitest.config.ts",
      "include": ["properties/**/*.test.ts", "spec/**/*.test.ts"],
      "exclude": ["**/*.int.test.ts", "spec/**/*.browser.test.{ts,tsx}", "spec/**/*.smoke.test.ts"],
      "database": false,
      "browser": false
    },
    {
      "name": "spec-int",
      "dir": "test",
      "config": "vitest.integration.config.ts",
      "include": ["spec/**/*.int.test.ts", "acceptance/**/*.test.ts", "smoke/**/*.int.test.ts"],
      "exclude": [],
      "database": true,
      "browser": false
    },
    {
      "name": "spec-browser",
